<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leopold I, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1640">1640</a>–<a href="/years/1705">1705</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leopold I was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> from 1658 to 1705. His reign saw the Ottoman siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> in 1683 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-turkish-war">Great Turkish War</a>, in which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> reconquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, and long wars against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a>. To win support he created new princely titles and in 1692 a ninth electorate for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hanover">House of Hanover</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leopold-i-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Leopold I, Holy Roman Emperor" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Benjamin Block · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Benjamin_von_Block_001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The forces of <b>Leopold I, Holy Roman Emperor</b>, under Charles of Lorraine met the army of Sultan Mehmed IV under the Grand Vizier Sarı Süleyman Pasha at Mohács, in the battle also called Harsány Mountain.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/august-12">12 August in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Duke Ernest Augustus of Brunswick-Lüneburg, ruling from Hanover, was granted a ninth electoral dignity by <b>Emperor Leopold</b> I in 1692 in return for military support, though it was recognised by the Imperial Diet only in 1708.</blockquote><a href="/state/electorate-of-hanover">Electorate of Hanover</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1692 <b>Emperor Leopold</b> I made Ernest Augustus an elector, and Calenberg became the core of the Electorate of Hanover, which absorbed the Principality of Lüneburg in 1705.</blockquote><a href="/state/principality-of-calenberg">Principality of Calenberg</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1599 the family was raised to the rank of imperial counts, and in 1670 Johann Adolf von Schwarzenberg, a senior adviser of <b>Emperor Leopold</b> I, was made a prince of the Empire, with the lands around Scheinfeld forming the core of the family's immediate territory.</blockquote><a href="/state/principality-of-schwarzenberg">Principality of Schwarzenberg</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/austria">Austria</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/austria">Austria</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=48.21,16.37&amp;year=1682" aria-label="Vienna on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4931 477 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Leopold I, Holy Roman Emperor"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5381 747h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5381 747h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=48.21,16.37&amp;year=1682">What was here in 1682? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
